The '''Bazaar''' is a commodity market for trading items. It is accessed through {{NPCSprite|Bazaar;Bazaar}} located in the {{Zone|Bazaar Alley}}, or with the {{Code|/bazaar}} [[Commands|command]] if the player has a {{ID|Booster Cookie}} active. {{SBL|7}} is required to access the Bazaar.

== Mechanics ==
The '''Bazaar''' is a commodity market, where players may buy and sell commodity items such as {{ID|Enchanted Rotten Flesh}}, {{ID|Null Sphere}} and {{ID|Super Compactor 3000}} for a price determined by market supply and demand, no one individual has a control over it. Items tradable in the Bazaar cannot be sold on the [[Auction House]].

The '''Bazaar''' is split into {{g|5}} categories: {{yellow|Farming}}, {{aqua|Mining}}, {{red|Combat}}, {{gold|Woods & Fishes}}, and {{Pink|Oddities}}. Clicking on a category will show all the item types or item categories within the category, as well as their buy and sell price. If an item type has multiple products, such as [[Diamond]], clicking it again will show all the different types of products under that item type, and their buy and sell prices. Due to limited number of slots, some items are grouped together under one umbrella category, for example all [[Gemstone]] types can be found under '''Gemstones''' and resources originating in [[Dwarven Mines]] under '''Dwarven Mines'''.

A toggle is available between ''Direct'' and ''Advanced modes''. In Direct mode, only the buy and sell prices of items are shown. In Advanced mode, the number and volume of buy orders and sell offers, as well as the number of instant buys and instant sells within the last {{g|7}} days are additionally shown.

=== Trading ===
====Types of trades====
Upon clicking into a specific product, {{g|4}} trading options are available: ''{{g|Buy Instantly}}'', ''{{gold|Sell Instantly}}'', ''{{g|Create Buy Order}}'' and ''{{gold|Create Sell Offer}}''.

Placing an ''{{g|Instant Buy}}'' request first requires the desired quantity of items. A player cannot instant buy more items than their inventory can hold ({{g|71,680}} [[Essence]], up to {{g|2,240}} for most items, {{g|560}} for items such as {{ID|Ender Pearl}}s and {{g|35}} for items that have stacks of 1 item,). Confirming the {{g|Instant Buy}} will purchase the items from the current cheapest sell offers available. The '''Bazaar''' will quote a price {{g|4%}} higher than the cheapest sell offer, so that a small change in offers does not restart the buy process. If the order goes through at a price below the additional {{g|4%}}, the extra {{c}} are refunded.<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/HypixelSkyblock/comments/ll3ury/cookies_for_ironman_are_apparently_coming_soon/gnna1x6?utm_source=share&utm_medium=web2x&context=3</ref> If the offers change too much, the purchase will fail and coins will be refunded.

''{{gold|Instantly Selling}}'' products takes all items from the inventory and sells them to the best {{G|Buy Orders}} automatically. Right-clicking the Instant Sell button allows the selection of quantity of items to {{gold|Instantly Sell}}.

Creating a ''{{g|Buy Order}}'' first requires the desired quantity of items. Clicking the sign allows the purchase of up to {{g|{{Abbr|71,680|1,120 stacks}}}} of that item in a single offer, or {{g|256}} for unstackable items. Three preset quantities are also available. For most stackable items, they are {{g|64}}, {{g|160}} and {{g|1,024}}; for most unstackable items, they are {{g|1}}, {{g|4}} and {{g|64}}. 

Upon choosing a quantity, a unit price for the order must be set. Three preset options are available: the same as the current highest buy order, {{c|0.1}} more than the highest buy order, and {{g|5%}} of the difference between the lowest sell price and highest buy price. A custom price can also be set with the sign.{{Info Needed|There is a limit to what price can be set, idk what it is}}

After the quantity and unit price are set, the order will be placed. Players who sell products of that type will fill the order.

Creating a ''{{gold|Sell Offer}}'' is similar. Clicking the {{gold|Sell Offer}} button will ask for a price, which can be matching the best offer, {{c|0.1}} below the best offer, {{g|10%}} of the difference between the lowest sell price and highest buy price, and a custom price. Upon confirming, all items from the inventory (or all of that Essence type, the player has) will be put up on {{gold|Sell Offer}}, and players will be able to buy them. By Right-clicking the Create Sell Order button, players can choose a specific amount of how many items to sell.

====Trading Features====
In the '''Bazaar''' main menu, the ''{{g|Sell Inventory Now}}'' option {{gold|instantly sells}} all '''Bazaar''' items in their inventory (Essence excluded) and the ''{{aqua|Sell Sacks Now}}'' option will sell all items in their [[Sacks]]. Within the menu of each specific item, players can choose to ignore the given product, doing so will prevent it from being {{g|Instantly Sold}} ({{g|sell orders}} can still be created).

Any active {{g|Buy Orders}} and {{Gold|Sell Offers}} can be managed with the Manage Orders menu. Here, the active {{g|Buy Orders}} and {{Gold|Sell Offers}} can be viewed. The number of items and {{c}} collected, the {{g|%}} completion and the top vendors of that order can be seen. Items and {{c}} can be collected with left click. Right clicking on an order allows it to be cancelled, provided no goods or {{c}} are left to claim on it. {{g|Buy orders}} which are fully filled can additionally be flipped to sell offer for a set price.

Buy orders and sell offers expire after {{g|7 days}}, after which the unused {{c}} or unsold items can be reclaimed.

A maximum of {{g|14}} orders and offers can be placed at once. The [[Account Upgrades#Bazaar Flipper|Bazaar Flipper perk]] (obtainable at the [[Community Shop]]) increases this number by {{g|7}} per level up to {{g|14}}, to a total of {{g|28}}. In addition, a maximum of {{c|1B|Short=yes}} worth of items can be placed on sell offer at once.

There is a {{g|1.25%}} tax on all '''Bazaar''' sales. The [[Account Upgrades#Bazaar Flipper|Bazaar Flipper perk]] decreases this tax by {{g|-0.125%}} per level up to {{g|-0.25%}}, making the tax {{g|1%}}.

Clicking on View Graphs in the product view will show a collection of graphs relating to the product. The graph of buy price, sell price, buy order volume, sell offer volume, instant sell volume, instant buy volume, instant sell moving {{c}}, and instant buy moving {{c}} can be seen. The range of these graphs can be changed between {{g|24 hours}}, {{g|7 days}} and {{g|31 days}} by left clicking; the graph can be enlarged with right click. It is not recommended to use the graph as a prediction table as it has a delay of around one day.

